  "info": {
    "title": "Supply line: order-rate management game",
    "category": "Games",
    "description": "A one-echelon, beer-game-style supply line: Inventory is replenished from a Supply Line pipeline through a 3rd-order shipping delay (DELAY3); customer demand steps up in week 5. A negative Inventory level IS the backlog, so one stock covers both. Every week a Policy-mode DECIDE ('order') asks the player to set the order rate low/medium/high, with a finer control beside it; Total Cost accumulates holding and backorder cost. In the results, read on-hand inventory against backlog, total cost and the service level.",
    "author": "Naga example"
  },
